# Kernel config fragment — Orange Pi 3 LTS (Allwinner H6, arm64) HEADLESS
# APPLIANCE. EXPERIMENTAL PLATFORM — see specs-orangepi3-lts/README.md: this
# board has NEVER been booted with an image from this repo. Every H6-specific
# symbol below is researched (web + kernel upstream source, incl. direct fetch
# of live mainline Linux/U-Boot source trees), NOT hardware-verified; treat
# every "verify" note as a real gap a reviewer must close before trusting this
# on real hardware.
#
# Applied on top of the chosen base defconfig by build-orangepi3-lts-stage4.sh
# using scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh (the Frite/Jetson/Orange-Pi-5 convention
# — real Kconfig dependency-aware merging — NOT the x86/RPi5 `scripts/config
# --action` replay DSL). Three jobs:
#   1) Keep the SAME hardening posture as the rest of the fleet (SELinux LSM,
#      lockdown-friendly, audit) — the SELinux guard in the builder enforces it.
#   2) Enable H6 platform + USB (incl. the H6's USB3 pipeline) + USB Ethernet
#      + storage (microSD + the onboard 8GB eMMC) so the board actually boots
#      and is reachable over the network. NOTE: unlike the Zero 2 template
#      there is NO working ONBOARD-Ethernet leg here — see the Networking
#      section below for why the jack is dead on the mainline DTB.
#   3) LUKS2/dm-crypt (--encrypt-root) + the squashfs/overlay live-boot bits.
#
# ── DELIBERATELY ABSENT: NO GPU/DRM/display config, NO framebuffer console ────
# IMPORTANT HONESTY NOTE — this is a DIFFERENT justification than the Zero 2
# template's. The H616/H618 siblings are headless because mainline has ZERO
# display-driver support for their DE33 display engine — a hard gap. The H6 is
# NOT in that situation: mainline DOES carry a DE3 mixer + the H6 DW-HDMI
# wrapper in drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/ (CONFIRMED — sun8i_mixer/sun8i-dw-hdmi
# with H6 compatibles), and the mainline sun50i-h6-orangepi-3.dts even ships
# an ENABLED &hdmi node. Staying headless here is a SCOPE decision, made for
# three honest reasons (see specs-orangepi3-lts/README.md for the full trail):
#   1) PARTIAL support: the mainline H6 display pipeline is real but rough for
#      an appliance-grade default (a history of HDMI/DDC quirks on this exact
#      board family — the OPi3's DDC bus sits behind a PH2-gated regulator —
#      and no GPU/accel story this image would ever use).
#   2) The DTB this image boots is the PLAIN Orange Pi 3's (mainline has no
#      -lts DTS at all — see the README's board-constants delta), so even the
#      display wiring is only ASSUMED identical on the LTS revision — exactly
#      the kind of unvalidated surface this EXPERIMENTAL platform must not
#      silently depend on.
#   3) Template parity: this platform is a faithful derivation of the Zero 2
#      HEADLESS APPLIANCE (one role, flavor-only, no desktop axis anywhere in
#      the four build channels); giving it a desktop mode would be a redesign,
#      not a port.
# DO NOT add CONFIG_DRM/CONFIG_DRM_SUN4I/CONFIG_FB*/CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE
# here by copy-paste habit from another platform's fragment — nothing in this
# image ever draws a pixel; revisit the scope in the README first if that ever
# changes.
#
# Format: standard .config fragment (CONFIG_FOO=y / # CONFIG_FOO is not set /
# CONFIG_FOO="string") — consumed by merge_config.sh, NOT by scripts/config.

# ── Allwinner sunxi platform (H6 shares this arm64 platform-select symbol
# with every other Allwinner SoC generation — H3/H5/H6/H616/...) ──────────────
CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI=y

# ── eMMC / microSD (Allwinner sunxi MMC host controller) ───────────────────
# CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI is the mainline driver for Allwinner's SD/MMC host
# controller IP — the H6's "allwinner,sun50i-h6-mmc"/"-emmc" compatibles are
# handled by the same sunxi-mmc driver. UNLIKE the Zero 2/Zero 3 siblings this
# board HAS an onboard 8GB eMMC, and the mainline sun50i-h6-orangepi-3.dts
# enables all three hosts (CONFIRMED by direct fetch): mmc0 = microSD slot,
# mmc1 = the SDIO WiFi module (inert here — no driver for the LTS's radio, see
# below), mmc2 = the eMMC (8-bit, non-removable). One driver covers them all.
CONFIG_MMC=y
CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI=y

# ── SPI: DELIBERATELY ABSENT (a real difference from the Zero 2 template) ──
# The Zero 2/Zero 2W/Zero 3 trees enable CONFIG_SPI_SUN6I/CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NOR
# for their mainline-DT-visible onboard SPI NOR boot flash. The mainline
# sun50i-h6-orangepi-3.dts enables NO &spi node at all (CONFIRMED by direct
# fetch), so those symbols would compile drivers that can never bind on the
# DTB this image boots — dead config, dropped by the same honesty rule that
# keeps the radio uncompiled below. (The LTS revision boots from microSD/eMMC;
# whether it even carries a NOR chip is vendor-sheet ambiguous — VERIFY on
# hardware before ever wiring SPI back in.)

# ── USB (H6: 1x USB2 OTG (musb) + ehci0/ohci0 + ehci3/ohci3 USB2 hosts + a
# genuine USB3 pipeline — dwc3/xhci behind the H6's own USB3 PHY; the mainline
# sun50i-h6-orangepi-3.dts enables &dwc3 + &usb3phy + both ehci/ohci pairs +
# &usb2otg, CONFIRMED by direct fetch). The USB3 leg is a REAL addition over
# the USB2-only H616 template — and it matters here, because USB Ethernet is
# this appliance's primary network path (see Networking below).
CONFIG_USB=y
CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=y
CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD_PLATFORM=y
CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD_PLATFORM=y
CONFIG_USB_MUSB_HDRC=y
CONFIG_USB_MUSB_SUNXI=y
CONFIG_USB_XHCI_HCD=y
CONFIG_USB_XHCI_PLATFORM=y
CONFIG_USB_DWC3=y
CONFIG_PHY_SUN50I_USB3=y
CONFIG_USB_STORAGE=y

# ── Networking: USB-Ethernet-FIRST — the onboard GbE jack is DEAD on the
# mainline DTB (the single biggest honest difference from the Zero 2 template).
# CONFIRMED by direct fetch: the mainline sun50i-h6-orangepi-3.dts ships NO
# ethernet/&emac/mdio node AT ALL — the plain OPi3's enable-ethernet DT patch
# (RTL8211E behind TWO supplies that must rise together — a wiring mainline's
# single phy-supply binding cannot express cleanly) was posted repeatedly and
# never landed. And the LTS revision swapped the PHY again (a Motorcomm
# YT8531C per the vendor sheet / Armbian's out-of-tree sun50i-h6-orangepi-3-lts
# DTS), so even that unlanded patch would pin the WRONG PHY here. Net result:
# on the DTB this image boots, the physical GbE jack does not exist as far as
# the kernel is concerned. This appliance is therefore USB-Ethernet-first —
# the SAME posture as the jack-less Orange Pi Zero 2W, same class set:
#   - CONFIG_USB_USBNET + CDCETHER/CDC_NCM: the generic USB-CDC classes most
#     USB Ethernet adapters (and phone-tether NCM) present.
#   - CONFIG_USB_RTL8152: Realtek RTL8152/RTL8153 (the most common USB GbE).
#   - CONFIG_USB_NET_AX88179_178A: ASIX AX88179/178A USB3-GbE family.
# The dwmac/stmmac stack + BOTH candidate PHY drivers are ALSO kept below —
# they are inert against the stock DTB (nothing to bind), but they are all
# mainline drivers, and they are exactly what makes a user-supplied
# -lts DTS/overlay (e.g. Armbian's, dropped in via extlinux's FDT line) light
# the jack up WITHOUT a kernel rebuild. Kept deliberately; labeled honestly.
CONFIG_NET=y
CONFIG_ETHERNET=y
CONFIG_USB_USBNET=y
CONFIG_USB_NET_CDCETHER=y
CONFIG_USB_NET_CDC_NCM=y
CONFIG_USB_RTL8152=y
CONFIG_USB_NET_AX88179_178A=y
# Inert-by-default onboard-GbE stack (see the honesty note above):
CONFIG_NET_VENDOR_STMICRO=y
CONFIG_STMMAC_ETH=y
CONFIG_STMMAC_PLATFORM=y
CONFIG_DWMAC_SUN8I=y
CONFIG_PHYLIB=y
CONFIG_MOTORCOMM_PHY=y
CONFIG_REALTEK_PHY=y

# ── WiFi/Bluetooth: DELIBERATELY NOT BUILT for the onboard radio ───────────
# The LTS revision's onboard radio is a Unisoc UWE5622 WiFi+BT combo module
# (per the vendor's own spec sheet — the same die as the Zero 2 sibling's
# "AW859A" package; the PLAIN OPi3 shipped a Broadcom AP6256 instead, which is
# why the mainline DTB carries brcm wifi/bt nodes — those bind NOTHING on the
# LTS's Unisoc part and are inert here). CONFIRMED (research inherited from
# the Zero 2/Zero 2W siblings): there is NO mainline kernel.org driver for the
# UWE5622 at all — not even a rough/incomplete one (unlike Orange Pi 5's
# AP6275P, which at
# least has an upstream brcmfmac-class driver with known rough edges). The only
# working driver is Unisoc/Allwinner's own out-of-tree BSP module source. There
# is therefore NOTHING to gain by enabling CONFIG_CFG80211/CONFIG_MAC80211/a
# brcmfmac-class module here — no in-tree driver would ever bind to this chip.
# This board is headless + Ethernet-first anyway (see the README), so the
# onboard radio is simply left uncompiled rather than carrying dead module
# config for hardware nothing in mainline can drive. A USB WiFi dongle with its
# OWN mainline driver would still work via the arm64 base defconfig's own
# module set (unrelated to this fragment) — see harden_radios() in the builder
# for the generic cfg80211/mac80211/bluetooth/btusb modprobe-blacklist posture
# that applies to any such dongle, same as every other platform in this repo.

# ── Hardware crypto (ARMv8 Crypto Extensions on the H6's 4x Cortex-A53
# cores) — same core as Orange Pi 5's LITTLE cluster, so the same guaranteed
# accelerator applies here. ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE_BLK=y

# ── LUKS2 root (dm-crypt) — --encrypt-root builds ──────────────────────────
# Same CONFIG_MD/BLK_DEV_DM/DM_CRYPT/CRYPTO_XTS/CRYPTO_AES pattern every other
# platform in this repo uses (x86/frite/rpi5/jetson/orangepi5). CONFIG_MD gates
# the whole drivers/md/Kconfig subtree that BLK_DEV_DM/DM_CRYPT depend on
# (directly or transitively) — without it, `make olddefconfig` silently drops
# them regardless of what's requested here.
CONFIG_MD=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_DM=y
CONFIG_DM_CRYPT=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_XTS=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA512=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_HASH=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_SKCIPHER=y
# Disable hibernation — resume-from-disk bypasses LUKS2 disk encryption.
# Mirrors every other hardened-*.config in this repo.
# CONFIG_HIBERNATION is not set

# ── Hardening posture (MUST match the fleet; guarded by the builder) ───────
# SECURITY_NETWORK must come before SECURITY_SELINUX — selinux depends on it.
CONFIG_SECURITY=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_NETWORK=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX_BOOTPARAM=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_YAMA=y
CONFIG_AUDIT=y
CONFIG_AUDITSYSCALL=y
CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL=y
CONFIG_LSM="yama,selinux,bpf"
# ASLR / stack / slab hardening
CONFIG_RANDOMIZE_BASE=y
CONFIG_STACKPROTECTOR_STRONG=y
CONFIG_SLAB_FREELIST_HARDENED=y
CONFIG_SLAB_FREELIST_RANDOM=y
CONFIG_HARDENED_USERCOPY=y
CONFIG_FORTIFY_SOURCE=y

# ── tun + iptables (tailscale needs /dev/net/tun + nf) ─────────────────────
CONFIG_TUN=y
CONFIG_NETFILTER=y
CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK=y
CONFIG_IP_NF_IPTABLES=y
CONFIG_NETFILTER_XTABLES=y

# ── Squashfs + overlay + loop (the LIVE flavor boots a squashfs) ───────────
# Same dmsquash-live boot design as Frite/RPi5/Orange-Pi-5: the LIVE/INSTALLER
# medium boots a dracut dmsquash-live initramfs that mounts LiveOS/squashfs.img
# read-only (loop + squashfs) and stacks a writable overlay = the ephemeral root.
CONFIG_SQUASHFS=y
CONFIG_SQUASHFS_XZ=y
CONFIG_OVERLAY_FS=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_LOOP=y
CONFIG_ISO9660_FS=y
CONFIG_DM_SNAPSHOT=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM=y
CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=y
CONFIG_DEVTMPFS_MOUNT=y
CONFIG_TMPFS=y
CONFIG_TMPFS_POSIX_ACL=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD=y

# ── Serial console ONLY — no framebuffer console (see the header note) ────
# Plain 8250-family UART support for the debug UART (mainline devicetree:
# aliases { serial0 = &uart0; }; chosen { stdout-path = "serial0:115200n8"; } —
# CONFIRMED against the live upstream sun50i-h6-orangepi-3.dts fetched for
# this port). CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_DW is the DesignWare 8250 variant Allwinner's
# UART IP uses upstream.
CONFIG_SERIAL_8250=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_DW=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_OF_PLATFORM=y
# Deliberately DISABLED: CONFIG_FB, CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE, CONFIG_DRM* —
# see the header. This board has no console beyond the serial UART. These
# MUST be explicit "is not set" directives, not just omitted from this
# fragment: the generic arm64 defconfig this builder starts from ships all
# three =y by default, and merge_config.sh only OVERRIDES a base default when
# a fragment says so explicitly — silently omitting a symbol leaves the base
# default untouched. (An earlier version of this fragment relied on omission
# alone, which left CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE=y in the final .config and
# tripped the builder's own post-olddefconfig guard on every real build.)
# CONFIG_DRM is not set
# CONFIG_FB is not set
# CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE is not set
